    "#| include: false\n",
    "import sys; sys.path.append(\"../../assets\")\n",
    "from mma import *\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import statsmodels.formula.api as smf\n",
    "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
    "from statsmodels.stats.outliers_influence import variance_inflation_factor\n",
    "import warnings; warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\"figure.figsize\": (8, 4), \"axes.spines.top\": False,\n",
    "                     \"axes.spines.right\": False, \"font.size\": 11})\n",
    "df = load_panel(\"../../data/mmm/alpenglow_weekly.csv\")\n",
    "df = add_fourier(df, order=2)\n",
    "df[\"log_sales\"] = np.log(df.sales_units_k)\n",
    "df[\"log_price\"] = np.log(df.price_eur)\n",
    "meta = pd.read_csv(\"../../data/mmm/country_meta.csv\")\n",
    "FULL = (\"log_sales ~ log_price + promo_share + xmas + easter + valentine \"\n",
    "        \"+ sin_1 + cos_1 + sin_2 + cos_2 + t\")\n",
    "de = df[df.country == \"DE\"]\n",
    "pl = df[df.country == \"PL\"]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2bf8009b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Welcome\n",
    "\n",
    "- Five Tuesdays, one company, one final decision: Alpenglow's 2027 media budget\n",
    "- Today: the toolkit and the regression you will use in every session\n",
    "- Lecture 60 min, guided lab 90 min, team exercise 60 min, debrief and quiz\n",
    "- You will not write Python from scratch: you specify, run, read, check, communicate\n",
    "- Everything lives in GitHub and renders with Quarto\n",
    "- Bring questions about setup to the clinic in the first 20 minutes\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.notes}\n",
    "Open with the arc of the course: Session 1 builds the regression toolkit, Sessions 2 and 3 turn it into a marketing mix model for one and then six countries, Session 4 asks whether we can trust it, Session 5 is the board meeting. Make the point that the single running case means every dataset they see describes the same company, so by Session 5 they know the business as well as the model.\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "## The company: Alpenglow\n",
    "\n",
    "- Vienna-based premium chocolate brand, founded 40 years ago\n",
    "- Six markets: Austria, Germany, France, Italy, Netherlands, Poland\n",
    "- Weekly data 2023 to 2025: units, revenue, price, promotion, distribution, media\n",
    "- Oldest market Austria (40 years), youngest Poland (4 years)\n",
    "- Germany is five times the Austrian volume; Poland grows fastest\n",
    "- All data are synthetic, with a truth the instructor reveals in Session 5\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.notes}\n",
    "Students need the business facts before the statistics. Stress that Poland is a young, fast-growing, lower-income market with the lowest shelf price. The question \"Is our price too high?\" sounds odd for the cheapest market until you relate price to income.\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "## Decision of the day\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.decision}\n",
    "**Is our price too high in Poland?**\n",
    "The Polish country manager wants a 10 % list-price cut. Finance says Poland already has the lowest price in the group. You have three years of weekly data for six countries. What does the data say about price sensitivity, and how sure are you?\n",
    ":::"
   ]
  },
