    "- Price elasticity -1.40 (95 % CI -2.04 to -0.76); promotion +0.45; R² 0.95\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.notes}\n",
    "Read the coefficients as business statements. Price: a 1 % increase cuts units by 1.4 %. Promotion: 10 percentage points more volume on promotion lifts units by about 4.5 %, net of the price cut that comes with it. Christmas adds about 5 % on top of the seasonal curve. The confidence interval for price is wide because, once promotion and trend are controlled, little price variation is left. That is a fact about the data, not a failure of the model.\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "## Elasticities for all six countries"
   ]
